  "diagnosis_text": "### Diagnosis\n\nThe fault is localized to the **s1\u2013s2 inter-switch link**:\n\n- Configured path from **h1 to h5** is:\n  `h1 \u2013 s4 \u2013 s2 \u2013 s1 \u2013 s3 \u2013 s6 \u2013 h5`\n- ONOS sees only **5 active inter-switch links**, while 6 are configured; the missing link is **s1 port 1 \u2194 s2 port 1**.\n- Both corresponding ports are disabled:\n  - `s1-eth1`: `enabled=false`, peer `s2:1`\n  - `s2-eth1`: `enabled=false`, peer `s1:1`\n- The h1-to-h5 ping has 100% loss.\n- Local connectivity is otherwise demonstrated:\n  - `h1 \u2192 h3`: succeeds through `s4\u2013s2\u2013s5`\n  - `h6 \u2192 h5`: succeeds on s6\n  - `h1 \u2192 h7`: also fails, consistent with traffic needing the same s2\u2013s1 segment.\n\nThe flow table does contain forwarding for h5 toward **s2 port 1**, but that port is down, so forwarding cannot cross the link.\n\n**Next step:** inspect or restore the operational/admin state of the `s1-eth1`/`s2-eth1` link and its underlying Mininet interfaces.",
